-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, "Offences affecting life"
-- (ss 299-311) and "Causing miscarriage; injuries to unborn children;
-- exposure of infants; and concealment of births" (ss 312-318).
--
-- Covers: s 299 (culpable homicide), s 300 with Exceptions 1-7 (murder),
-- ss 302(1), 302(2), 304(a), 304(b), 304A(a), 304A(b), 305(1)(a)-(c), 306,
-- 307(1), 307(2), 308, 308B, 312, 313, 317, 318.
-- Deferred (notes/body-a-coverage.md): ss 301, 304B, 304C, 308A, 310, 311,
-- 314, 315, 316. s 303 does not exist; s 309 is repealed.
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt).
--
-- What a reader must know before reading:
--
-- * Murder is culpable homicide (s 299) that meets a limb of s 300 and falls
--   within none of its Exceptions. The Exceptions are part of s 300 itself,
--   not general exceptions (PLAN.md §5), so they are in the ladder, each its
--   own exported rule. An Exception is for the accused to bring himself
--   within; an unknown Exception leaf is FALSE, so a murder charge frames
--   unless one is established. That is the Code's burden, not a default.
-- * s 304A reads `Rash Act Facts`, declared in pc-body-a-hurt.l4 beside
--   ss 336-338, which punish the same conduct by its lesser results.
-- * s 301 (transferred description) is a deeming rule with no charge of its
--   own; the reference row's culpable-homicide-301.l4 encodes it and it is
--   not repeated here (deferred, F-9).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-hurt`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, Offences affecting life (ss 299-311)`

§§ `The facts of one homicide, or attempt`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 299, 300, 302, 304, 307, 308 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Homicide Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person killed (or, for ss 307-308, the person whose death was intended), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by stabbing the said Z in the chest with a knife"
    -- s 299
    `causes death by doing an act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused's act cause the victim's death? Accelerating the death of someone already ill is causing it (Explanation 1); so is causing a bodily injury from which death follows although proper treatment might have prevented it (Explanation 2). Killing a child in the womb is not homicide; killing a living child any part of whom has been brought forth may be (Explanation 3).
    `with the intention of causing death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused do the act intending to cause death? (ss 299, 300(a), 304(a), 307, 308)
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend to cause a bodily injury that is likely to cause death? (ss 299, 304(a))
    `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused know that the act was likely to cause death? (ss 299, 304(b))
    -- s 300 (b)-(d)
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom the harm is caused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend a bodily injury he knew to be likely to kill this particular victim - for example because he knew of the victim's disease? (s 300(b), illus (b))
    `with the intention of causing bodily injury to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend to cause the bodily injury that was in fact inflicted? (s 300(c))
    `the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that injury sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death? An objective question. (s 300(c))
    `knows that the act is so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death, or such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused know the act was so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death or likely-fatal injury? (s 300(d))
    `commits such act without any excuse for incurring the risk of causing death or such injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do the act without any excuse for running that risk? (s 300(d))
    -- s 300 Exception 1
    `whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused deprived of self-control by grave and sudden provocation? A question of fact: would an ordinary person of the same gender and age, sharing characteristics affecting its gravity, be so deprived (Explanation 1)? Words, gestures or conduct will do (Explanation 2).
    `causes the death of the person who gave the provocation, or of any other person by mistake or accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person killed the one who gave the provocation, or another person killed by mistake or accident? (Exception 1)
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provocation NOT sought or voluntarily provoked by the accused as an excuse? (Exception 1 proviso (a))
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused neither know nor have reason to believe that the provocation came from something done in obedience to the law or by a public servant lawfully exercising his powers? (Exception 1 proviso (b))
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provocation NOT given by something done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence? (Exception 1 proviso (c))
    -- s 300 Exception 2
    `in the exercise of the right of private defence of person or property, exceeds the power given to him by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused exercising the right of private defence of person or property, and did he exceed the power the law gave him? (Exception 2)
    `causes the death of the person against whom he is exercising such right of defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person killed the one against whom he was defending? (Exception 2)
    `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances which gave rise to the act of private defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there NO intention, formed before the circumstances giving rise to the private defence, to cause death (s 300(a)) or injury of the kind in s 300(b) or (c), or to do an act known to be imminently dangerous (s 300(d))? (Exception 2 Explanation)
    `without any intention of doing more harm than is necessary for the purpose of such defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused NOT intend more harm than was necessary for the defence? (Exception 2)
    -- s 300 Exception 3
    `being a public servant, or aiding a public servant acting for the advancement of public justice, exceeds the powers given to him by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused a public servant (or aiding one acting for the advancement of public justice) who exceeded his legal powers? (Exception 3)
    `causes death by doing an act which he, in good faith, believes to be lawful and necessary for the due discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did he cause death by an act he believed in good faith (s 26B) to be lawful and necessary for his duty? (Exception 3)
    `without ill will towards the person whose death is caused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did he act without ill will towards the person killed? (Exception 3)
    -- s 300 Exception 4
    `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances constituting the sudden fight` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there NO intention, formed before the sudden fight, of the kind s 300(a)-(d) describes? (Exception 4 Explanation 3)
    `in a sudden fight` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the killing in a sudden fight? A "fight" includes an exchange of blows even if they miss, and a single blow or punch (Explanation 2); a mutual stare is not a fight (illus (a)). It does not matter who gave the provocation or struck first (Explanation 1).
    `in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel? A quarrel needs no words (Explanation 4).
    `without the offender having taken undue advantage or acted in a cruel or unusual manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused NOT take undue advantage, and NOT act in a cruel or unusual manner? Kicking a motionless victim is undue advantage (illus (b)). (Exception 4)
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the person whose death was caused was acting in obedience to the law, or was a public servant acting in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused neither know nor have reason to believe that the deceased was acting in obedience to the law, or was a public servant acting lawfully? (Exception 4 proviso)
    -- s 300 Exception 5
    `the person whose death is caused is above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the deceased above 18 years of age? (Exception 5; the helper `above 18 years of age` decides it from the age)
    `suffers death or takes the risk of death with his own consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased suffer death, or take the risk of it, with his own consent (s 90)? (Exception 5)
    -- s 300 Exception 6
    `the offender being a woman voluntarily causes the death of her child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused a woman who voluntarily caused the death of her own child? (Exception 6)
    `the child is below 12 months of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child below 12 months of age? (Exception 6)
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time, was the balance of her mind disturbed because she had not fully recovered from giving birth to the child, or by the effect of lactation? (Exception 6)
    -- s 300 Exception 7
    `suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of the acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused suffering from an abnormality of mind (arrested or retarded development, inherent causes, or disease or injury) that substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of his acts or omissions in causing the death? (Exception 7(a)(i))
    `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... substantially impaired his capacity to know they were wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons? (Exception 7(a)(ii), and the paragraph below it, limb (a))
    `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong as contrary to law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... and to know they were wrong as contrary to law? (Exception 7(a)(ii), and the paragraph below it, limb (b))
    `suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions in causing the death? (Exception 7(b))
    -- ss 307, 308 - attempts
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the circumstances such that, had the act caused death, it would have been murder (s 300, no Exception)? (s 307)
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide not amounting to murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the circumstances such that, had the act caused death, it would have been culpable homicide not amounting to murder - for example on grave and sudden provocation (illus to s 308)? (s 308)
    `hurt is caused to any person by such act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause hurt (s 319) to anyone? (ss 307(1), 308)
    `under sentence of imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused, at the time, under sentence of imprisonment for life? (s 307(2))

§§ `s 299 - culpable homicide`

-- 299. Whoever causes death by doing an act with the intention of causing
--      death, or with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely
--      to cause death, or with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to
--      cause death, commits the offence of culpable homicide.
--      [Explanations 1-3 are in the @desc of `causes death by doing an act`.]
@export Whether the accused "commits the offence of culpable homicide" within section 299 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what he meant or foresaw by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits culpable homicide` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `causes death by doing an act`
    AND (    f's `with the intention of causing death`
         OR  f's `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death`
         OR  f's `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death` )

§§ `s 300 - murder`

-- 300. Except in the cases hereinafter excepted culpable homicide is murder -
--   (a) if the act by which the death is caused is done with the intention of
--       causing death;
--   (b) if it is done with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the
--       offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom
--       the harm is caused;
--   (c) if it is done with the intention of causing bodily injury to any
--       person, and the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in
--       the ordinary course of nature to cause death; or
--   (d) if the person committing the act knows that it is so imminently
--       dangerous that it must in all probability cause death, or such bodily
--       injury as is likely to cause death, and commits such act without any
--       excuse for incurring the risk of causing death, or such injury as
--       aforesaid.

@export Exception 1 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - grave and sudden provocation
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The provocation, and whom the accused killed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 1 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder if the offender"
    ... f's `whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation`
    ... f's `causes the death of the person who gave the provocation, or of any other person by mistake or accident`
    ... "subject to the following provisos: (a)"
    ... f's `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person`
    ... "(b)"
    ... f's `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`
    ... "(c)"
    ... f's `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`

@export Exception 2 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - exceeding the right of private defence
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The private defence, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 2 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder if the offender"
    ... f's `in the exercise of the right of private defence of person or property, exceeds the power given to him by law`
    ... "and"
    ... f's `causes the death of the person against whom he is exercising such right of defence`
    ... f's `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances which gave rise to the act of private defence`
    ... "and"
    ... f's `without any intention of doing more harm than is necessary for the purpose of such defence`

@export Exception 3 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - public servant exceeding his powers
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The public servant's duty and belief
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 3 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder if the offender,"
    ... f's `being a public servant, or aiding a public servant acting for the advancement of public justice, exceeds the powers given to him by law`
    ... "and"
    ... f's `causes death by doing an act which he, in good faith, believes to be lawful and necessary for the due discharge of his duty as such public servant`
    ... "and"
    ... f's `without ill will towards the person whose death is caused`

@export Exception 4 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - sudden fight
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The fight, and how the accused conducted himself in it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 4 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder if it is committed"
    ... f's `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances constituting the sudden fight`
    ... f's `in a sudden fight`
    ... f's `in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel`
    ... "and"
    ... f's `without the offender having taken undue advantage or acted in a cruel or unusual manner`
    ... "subject to the proviso that"
    ... f's `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the person whose death was caused was acting in obedience to the law, or was a public servant acting in the lawful exercise of his powers`

@export Exception 5 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - consent of a person above 18 years of age
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The deceased's age and consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 5 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder when the person whose death is caused, being"
    ... f's `the person whose death is caused is above 18 years of age`
    ... ","
    ... f's `suffers death or takes the risk of death with his own consent`

@export Exception 6 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - a mother's killing of her child below 12 months of age
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The mother, the child, and the balance of her mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 6 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder if"
    ... f's `the offender being a woman voluntarily causes the death of her child`
    ... "being a child"
    ... f's `the child is below 12 months of age`
    ... "and at the time of the offence"
    ... f's `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation`

@export Whether a child of the given age in months is "below 12 months of age" (s 300 Exception 6, s 310 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in completed months
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `below 12 months of age` months IF months < 12

@export Exception 7 to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 - abnormality of mind
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The accused's state of mind at the time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Exception 7 to section 300 applies` f IF
        "Culpable homicide is not murder if ... the offender was suffering from such abnormality of mind ... as substantially - (a) impaired the offender's capacity - (i)"
    ..  f's `suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of the acts or omissions`
    OR  "(ii) to know whether such acts or omissions are wrong - which applies only if there was a substantial impairment of the capacity to know that they (a) are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons; and (b) are wrong as contrary to law"
        ... f's `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons`
        ... f's `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong as contrary to law`
    OR  "(b) impaired the offender's power to control his acts or omissions"
    ..  f's `suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions`

@export Whether any of the Exceptions to section 300 of the Penal Code 1871 applies, so that culpable homicide is not murder
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The facts each Exception reads
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Exception to section 300 applies` f IF
        `Exception 1 to section 300 applies` f
    OR  `Exception 2 to section 300 applies` f
    OR  `Exception 3 to section 300 applies` f
    OR  `Exception 4 to section 300 applies` f
    OR  `Exception 5 to section 300 applies` f
    OR  `Exception 6 to section 300 applies` f
    OR  `Exception 7 to section 300 applies` f

@export Whether culpable homicide is "murder within the meaning of section 300(a)" of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant by it, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `murder within the meaning of section 300(a)` f IF
        "Except in the cases hereinafter excepted"
    AND NOT (`an Exception to section 300 applies` f)
    AND `commits culpable homicide` f
    AND "is murder - (a) if the act by which the death is caused is done"
    AND f's `with the intention of causing death`

@export Whether culpable homicide is "murder within the meaning of section 300(b)" of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant by it, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `murder within the meaning of section 300(b)` f IF
        "Except in the cases hereinafter excepted"
    AND NOT (`an Exception to section 300 applies` f)
    AND `commits culpable homicide` f
    AND "is murder - (b) if it is done"
    AND f's `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom the harm is caused`

@export Whether culpable homicide is "murder within the meaning of section 300(c)" of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant by it, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `murder within the meaning of section 300(c)` f IF
        "Except in the cases hereinafter excepted"
    AND NOT (`an Exception to section 300 applies` f)
    AND `commits culpable homicide` f
    AND "is murder - (c) if it is done"
    AND f's `with the intention of causing bodily injury to any person`
    AND "and"
    AND f's `the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death`

@export Whether culpable homicide is "murder within the meaning of section 300(d)" of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he knew of it, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `murder within the meaning of section 300(d)` f IF
        "Except in the cases hereinafter excepted"
    AND NOT (`an Exception to section 300 applies` f)
    AND `commits culpable homicide` f
    AND "is murder - (d) if the person committing the act"
    AND f's `knows that the act is so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death, or such bodily injury as is likely to cause death`
    AND "and"
    AND f's `commits such act without any excuse for incurring the risk of causing death or such injury`

@export Whether the accused "commits murder" within section 300 of the Penal Code 1871, under any of its limbs
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or knew, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits murder` f IF
        `murder within the meaning of section 300(a)` f
    OR  `murder within the meaning of section 300(b)` f
    OR  `murder within the meaning of section 300(c)` f
    OR  `murder within the meaning of section 300(d)` f

@export Whether the accused commits "culpable homicide not amounting to murder" (ss 299, 300 and 304 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or knew, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits culpable homicide not amounting to murder` f IF
        `commits culpable homicide` f
    ... "not amounting to"
    ... NOT (`commits murder` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of culpable homicide not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `causes death by doing an act`) "causes death by doing an act"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of causing death` OR f's `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` OR f's `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death`) "with the intention of causing death, or of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death, or with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death"))

GIVEN f    IS A `Homicide Facts`
      what IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the homicide recital` f what MEANS
    CONCAT "did commit ", what, " by causing the death of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`

§§ `s 301 - culpable homicide by causing the death of a person other than the person whose death was intended`

-- Deferred: a deeming rule with no charge of its own. The reference row's
-- culpable-homicide-301.l4 encodes it; see body-a-forks.md F-9.

§§ `s 302 - punishment for murder`

-- 302.-(1) Whoever commits murder within the meaning of section 300(a) shall
--      be punished with death.
--   (2) Whoever commits murder within the meaning of section 300(b), (c) or
--      (d) shall be punished with death or imprisonment for life and shall, if
--      he is not punished with death, also be liable to caning.
%%PUNISH 302(1) | death | S | - | - | | | - | - | | | - | | | F
%%PUNISH 302(2) | death or imprisonment for life and shall, if he is not punished with death, also be liable to caning | O | O | - | | | - | - | | | L | | | F

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 302(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (murder within the meaning of section 300(a))
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant by it, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 302(1)` f IF
        "Whoever commits"
    ... `murder within the meaning of section 300(a)` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 302(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (murder within the meaning of section 300(b), (c) or (d))
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or knew, and the Exceptions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 302(2)` f IF
        "Whoever commits murder within the meaning of section 300(b), (c) or (d)"
    ... (    `murder within the meaning of section 300(b)` f
         OR  `murder within the meaning of section 300(c)` f
         OR  `murder within the meaning of section 300(d)` f )

GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of murder not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`elements of culpable homicide not made out` f),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (`an Exception to section 300 applies` f)) "the case is not within any of the Exceptions to section 300"))

@export Frame a charge under section 302(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (murder), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 302(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "302(1)" "murder"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 302(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 302(1)` f)
        (`the homicide recital` f "murder")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of murder not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of causing death`) "the act by which the death is caused is done with the intention of causing death (s 300(a))")))

@export Frame a charge under section 302(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (murder), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 302(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "302(2)" "murder"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 302(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 302(2)` f)
        (`the homicide recital` f "murder")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of murder not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`murder within the meaning of section 300(b)` f OR `murder within the meaning of section 300(c)` f OR `murder within the meaning of section 300(d)` f) "a limb of section 300(b), (c) or (d)")))

-- [There is no section 303.]

§§ `s 304 - punishment for culpable homicide not amounting to murder`

-- 304. Whoever commits culpable homicide not amounting to murder shall -
--   (a) if the act by which death is caused is done with the intention of
--       causing death, or of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause
--       death, be punished with - (i) imprisonment for life, and shall also be
--       liable to caning; or (ii) imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--       20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning; or
--   (b) if the act is done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause death,
--       but without any intention to cause death, or to cause such bodily
--       injury as is likely to cause death, be punished with imprisonment for
--       a term which may extend to 15 years, or with fine, or with caning, or
