`charge under s 304(a)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "304(a)" "culpable homicide not amounting to murder"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 304(a)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 304(a)` f)
        (`the homicide recital` f "culpable homicide not amounting to murder")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of culpable homicide not amounting to murder not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of causing death` OR f's `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death`) "the act is done with the intention of causing death, or of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death")))

@export Frame a charge under section 304(b) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
