§§ `ss 305 and 306 - abetment of suicide or attempted suicide`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 305, 306 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Suicide Abetment Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person who committed or attempted suicide
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc How the accused abetted, as it is to read after "to wit,"
    `the person commits suicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person commit suicide? (ss 305(1)(a), 306)
    `the person attempts suicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person attempt suicide? (ss 305(1)(b), (c), 306)
    `abets the commission of such suicide or attempted suicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused abet it, within s 107 (instigating, engaging in a conspiracy for, or intentionally aiding it)? Abetment is general-part's to define; joined at integration.
    `the person is a minor or a person who lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person below 18 years of age, or lacking capacity to understand the consequences of attempting or committing suicide, from unsoundness of mind, mental incapacity, intoxication, or a drug or other substance? (s 305(2))
    `knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person was a minor or a person who lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused know, or ought he reasonably to have known, that? (s 305(1))
    `hurt is caused to any person in the course of the attempted suicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was hurt (s 319) caused to anyone in the course of the attempt? (s 305(1)(c))

-- 305.-(1) If any minor or other person who lacks capacity -
--   (a) commits suicide, whoever abets the commission of the suicide and who
--       knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who committed
--       suicide was a minor or a person who lacks capacity, shall be punished
