--       which may extend to 20 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to death
--       or imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine;
--   (b) attempts suicide, whoever abets the attempted suicide and who knew or
--       ought reasonably to have known [the same], shall be punished with
--       imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be
--       liable to fine; or
--   (c) attempts suicide and hurt is caused to any person in the course of the
--       attempted suicide, whoever abets the attempted suicide and who knew or
--       ought reasonably to have known [the same], shall be punished with
--       imprisonment for life or with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--       to 20 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for
--       life, also be liable to fine.
--   (2) "minor" means a person below 18 years of age; "person who lacks
--       capacity" means [see the @desc of the leaf].
