§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, Causing miscarriage; injuries to unborn children; exposure of infants; and concealment of births (ss 312-318)`

§§ `ss 312 and 313 - causing miscarriage`

-- 312. Subject to the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974,
--      whoever voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or
--      with fine, or with both; and if the woman's pregnancy is of more than
--      16 weeks' duration as calculated in accordance with section 4 of that
--      Act, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      7 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
--      Explanation.-A woman who causes herself to miscarry is within the
--      meaning of this section.
-- 313. Whoever commits the offence defined in section 312, without the consent
--      of the woman, whether the woman's pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks'
--      duration or not as mentioned in that section, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--      to 10 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life,
--      also be liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 312, 313 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Miscarriage Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the woman, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes her, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc How the miscarriage was caused, as it is to read after "to wit,"
    `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused voluntarily (s 26A) cause a pregnant woman to miscarry? A woman who causes herself to miscarry is within this (s 312 Explanation).
    `not a treatment authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it NOT a termination the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974 authorises? That Act is not encoded; the investigator answers it.
    `the woman's pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks' duration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the pregnancy of more than 16 weeks' duration, calculated under s 4 of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974? (s 312; the helper `more than 16 weeks' duration` decides it from the weeks)
    `without the consent of the woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done without the woman's consent? (s 313)

%%PUNISH 312 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both | - | - | O | 36 | | - | O | | | - | | | T
%%PUNISH 312, more than 16 weeks | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine | - | - | S | 84 | | - | L | | | - | | | F
%%PUNISH 313 | imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine | - | O | O | 120 | | - | L | | | - | | | F

@export Whether a pregnancy of the given number of weeks is "of more than 16 weeks' duration" (s 312 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER @desc The duration of the pregnancy in weeks, calculated under s 4 of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `more than 16 weeks' duration` weeks IF weeks > 16

@export Whether the accused commits "the offence defined in section 312" of the Penal Code 1871 (causing miscarriage)
GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Facts` @desc What the accused did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 312` f IF
        "Subject to the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974,"
    ... f's `not a treatment authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`
    ... "whoever"
    ... f's `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 313 of the Penal Code 1871 (causing miscarriage without the woman's consent)
GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Facts` @desc What the accused did, and whether the woman consented
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 313` f IF
        "Whoever commits the offence defined in section 312"
    ... `offence under s 312` f
    ... f's `without the consent of the woman`

GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of section 312 not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry`) "voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `not a treatment authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`) "not authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974"))

@export Frame a charge under section 312 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Facts` @desc The facts, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 312` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "312" "causing miscarriage"
        (IF f's `the woman's pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks' duration`
         THEN `punishment prescribed by s 312, more than 16 weeks`'s words
         ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 312`'s words)
        (`offence under s 312` f)
        (CONCAT "did voluntarily cause ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a woman with child, to miscarry",
                IF f's `the woman's pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks' duration` THEN ", her pregnancy being of more than 16 weeks' duration" ELSE "",
                ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of section 312 not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 313 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Facts` @desc The facts, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 313` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "313" "causing miscarriage without woman's consent"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 313`'s words)
        (`offence under s 313` f)
        (CONCAT "did, without her consent, voluntarily cause ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a woman with child, to miscarry, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of section 312 not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `without the consent of the woman`) "without the consent of the woman")))

