§§ `s 317 - exposure and abandonment of a child below 12 years of age`

-- 317. Whoever, being the father or mother of a child below 12 years of age,
--      or having the care of such child, exposes or leaves such child in any
--      place with the intention of wholly abandoning such child shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or
--      with fine, or with both.
--      Explanation.-This section is not intended to prevent the trial of the
--      offender for murder or culpable homicide as the case may be, if the
--      child dies in consequence of the exposure.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 317 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Child Exposure Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The child's name, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes the child, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc Where and how the child was left, as it is to read after "to wit,"
    `being the father or mother of the child, or having the care of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused the child's father or mother, or did he or she have the care of the child? (s 317)
    `the child is below 12 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child below 12 years of age? (s 317; the helper `below 12 years of age`)
    `exposes or leaves such child in any place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused expose or leave the child somewhere? (s 317)
    `with the intention of wholly abandoning such child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend to abandon the child wholly? (s 317)

%%PUNISH 317 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both | - | - | O | 84 | | - | O | | | - | | | T

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 317 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Child Exposure Facts` @desc Who the accused is to the child, and what he or she did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 317` f IF
        "Whoever,"
    ... f's `being the father or mother of the child, or having the care of the child`
    ... "a child"
    ... f's `the child is below 12 years of age`
    ... f's `exposes or leaves such child in any place`
    ... f's `with the intention of wholly abandoning such child`

@export Frame a charge under section 317 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Exposure Facts` @desc The facts, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 317` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "317" "exposure and abandonment of a child below 12 years of age by parent or person having care of it"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 317`'s words)
        (`offence under s 317` f)
        (CONCAT "being a parent of, or having the care of, ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a child below 12 years of age, did leave the said child with the intention of wholly abandoning the said child, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `being the father or mother of the child, or having the care of the child`) "being the father or mother of the child, or having the care of the child"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the child is below 12 years of age`) "a child below 12 years of age"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `exposes or leaves such child in any place`) "exposes or leaves such child in any place"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of wholly abandoning such child`) "with the intention of wholly abandoning such child")))

§§ `s 318 - concealment of birth by secret disposal of dead body`

-- 318. Whoever by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a
--      child, whether such child dies before or after or during its birth,
--      intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      2 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 318 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Concealment of Birth Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc How the body was disposed of, as it is to read after "to wit,"
    `by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused secretly bury, or otherwise dispose of, the dead body of a child - whether the child died before, during or after birth? (s 318)
    `intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused thereby intentionally conceal, or try to conceal, the child's birth? (s 318)

%%PUNISH 318 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both | - | - | O | 24 | | - | O | | | - | | | T

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 318 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Concealment of Birth Facts` @desc What the accused did with the body, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 318` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child`
    ... f's `intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child`

@export Frame a charge under section 318 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Concealment of Birth Facts` @desc The facts, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 318` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "318" "concealment of birth by secret disposal of dead body"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 318`'s words)
        (`offence under s 318` f)
        (CONCAT "did, by secretly disposing of the dead body of a child, intentionally conceal the birth of the said child, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child`) "by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child`) "intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child")))
